      "label": "第三层  核对推荐和安全的范围",
      "color": "#95723E"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000006",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 677,
      "y": 39,
      "width": 766,
      "height": 178,
      "text": "## 王同翰 Tonghan Wang\n\n**2024–2026｜30 篇论文和 1 篇博士论文**\n\n截至 2026-11-24，预印本与正式版合并。加粗标出本人综述和 6 篇直接研究广告的论文。\n\n[清华](https://collegeai.tsinghua.edu.cn/en/People/Full_time_PI/Tonghan_WANG.htm) · [作者主页](https://tonghanwang.github.io/) · [DBLP](https://dblp.org/pid/175/6039-1.html)",
      "color": "#64748B"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000007",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 34,
      "y": 306,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 470,
      "text": "## 2024｜7 篇\n\n- [Multi-Sender Persuasion: A Computational Perspective](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/hossain24c.html)\n- [Position: Social Environment Design Should be Further Developed for AI-based Policy-Making](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/zhang24cl.html)\n- [GemNet: Menu-Based, Strategy-Proof Multi-Bidder Auctions Through Deep Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.07428)\n- [Principal-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Orchestrating AI Agents with Contracts](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.18074)\n- [Multi-agent policy transfer via task relationship modeling](https://doi.org/10.1007/s11432-023-3862-1)\n- [The Bandit Whisperer: Communication Learning for Restless Bandits](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.05686)（AAAI 2025）\n- [On Diffusion Models for Multi-Agent Partial Observability: Shared Attractors, Error Bounds, and Composite Flow](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.13953)（AAMAS 2025）"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000009",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 556,
      "y": 306,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 470,
      "text": "## 2025｜7 篇＋博士论文\n\n- **[Automated Mechanism Design: A Survey](https://www.sigecom.org/exchanges/volume_22/2/CURRY.pdf)**（与 Michael J. Curry 合著）\n- [BundleFlow: Deep Menus for Combinatorial Auctions by Diffusion-Based Optimization](https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.15283)\n- [Robust Optimization with Diffusion Models for Green Security](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.05730)\n- [Adaptive Frontier Exploration on Graphs with Applications to Network-Based Disease Testing](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.21671)\n- [Composite Flow Matching for Reinforcement Learning with Shifted-Dynamics Data](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.23062)\n- [Translate Policy to Language: Flow Matching Generated Rewards for LLM Explanations](https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.12530)（ICLR 2026）\n- [Celebrating Diversity With Subtask Specialization in Shared Multiagent Reinforcement Learning](https://doi.org/10.1109/TNNLS.2023.3326744)（2025 卷期）\n- [Advancing Deep Learning for Multiagent AI: Mechanisms, Organizations, and Dynamics](https://dash.harvard.edu/entities/publication/a78c8389-7eb0-4e91-a0a7-d1f5d88ff8a5)（哈佛博士论文）"
    },
    {
      "id": "000000000000000b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1078,
      "y": 306,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 470,
      "text": "## 2026｜2–7 月，8 篇\n\n- [LLM Active Alignment: A Nash Equilibrium Perspective](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06836)\n- **[Incentive-Aware Multi-Fidelity Optimization for Generative Advertising in Large Language Models](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.06263)**（COLM 2026）\n- [The Memory Curse: How Expanded Recall Erodes Cooperative Intent in LLM Agents](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.08060)\n- **[LLM Advertisement based on Neuron Auctions](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.08326)**\n- [How LLMs Are Persuaded: A Few Attention Heads, Rerouted](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09314)\n- **[NaiAD: Initiate Data-Driven Research for LLM Advertising](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09918)**\n- [Duality for Optimal Multi-Item, Multi-Bidder Auction Design: Revenue Certificates through Deep Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.10112)（EC 2026）\n- **[PILA: Plug-and-Play Insertion for LLM-native Advertising](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25590)**"
    },
    {
      "id": "000000000000000d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1600,
      "y": 306,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 470,
      "text": "## 2026｜7–10 月，8 篇\n\n- **[Evaluating and Pricing Advertisements in AI-Generated Responses](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.27686)**\n- [Every Cache Entry Earns Its Place: Global Allocation of Resolution and Coverage for KV Cache Compression](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.07001)\n- [Verbalizing Multi-Token Concepts in LLMs](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.31084)\n- [Loyal Agents: Training LLM Agents to Protect Principal Interests Under Strategic Information Asymmetry](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.34714)\n- [A mechanistic study of language model introspection](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.35108)\n- [Growing and Transferring Pathways for LLM Reinforcement Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.16489)\n- **[DiffAuction: An Auction-Driven Framework for Generative Image Advertising](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.34917)**\n- [ACCT: Asymmetric Cross-LLM Context Transfer](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.42116)"
    },
    {
      "id": "000000000000000f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 732,
      "y": 986,
      "width": 656,
      "height": 144,
      "text": "## 用什么标准筛\n\n先找综述和领域概览。原始论文再看它是否直接回答广告怎么生成、怎么竞价、怎么评估，以及与推荐或安全有什么关系。",
      "color": "#64748B"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000014",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 34,
      "y": 1222,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 241,
      "text": "### 综述与领域入口\n\n**本人署名综述** · *Automated Mechanism Design: A Survey*\n\n**广告文献地图** · *NaiAD* 的相关工作，及其引用的 Feizi 等人的领域概览。\n\n这条线先用来判断已有工作怎样组织、我们的范围会不会重合。",
      "color": "#397766"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000015",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 556,
      "y": 1222,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 241,
      "text": "### 直接相关 · 生成式广告\n\n- **插入** · PILA\n- **竞价与分配** · Neuron Auctions、Multi-Fidelity\n- **数据、评估与定价** · NaiAD、Evaluating and Pricing\n- **生成图像广告** · DiffAuction",
      "color": "#396A9A"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000016",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1078,
      "y": 1222,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 241,
      "text": "### 相邻 · 推荐、安全与竞价背景\n\n- **推荐与用户利益** · Loyal Agents\n- **模型如何被影响** · How LLMs Are Persuaded\n- **一般竞价机制** · GemNet、BundleFlow、Duality\n\n写到对应问题时，再用这些工作补背景。",
      "color": "#95723E"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000017",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1600,
      "y": 1222,
      "width": 486,
      "height": 241,
      "text": "### 其余 · 了解作者的研究范围\n\n基础模型训练与推理、模型解释、多智能体强化学习，以及安全优化、疾病检测等应用。\n\n第一轮扫标题，暂时留在总表。",
      "color": "#697281"
    },
    {
      "id": "000000000000001c",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 17,
      "y": 1678,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 先读 Feizi 等的广告概览\n\n**领域观点文，王同翰的 NaiAD 引用了它。** 先读 §2 和 §4.5，记下广告系统怎么拆解，以及 token auction 和其他机制怎么放在一起比较。\n\n[Online Advertisements with LLMs: Opportunities and Challenges](https://www.sigecom.org/exchanges/volume_22/2/FEIZI.pdf)",
      "color": "#397766"
    },
    {
      "id": "000000000000001d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 17,
      "y": 1997,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 再读 NaiAD 的相关工作\n\n**§6.1–6.2** 分别梳理广告算法与机制、数据集与基准。在这两节标出宋卓、邓小铁和 Michael J. Curry 的相关论文线索。\n\n[NaiAD · §6 Related Works](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.09918v1#S6)",
      "color": "#397766"
    },
    {
      "id": "000000000000001e",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 17,
      "y": 2316,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 再补王同翰与 Curry 的综述\n\n**正式综述，SIGecom Exchanges 2025。** 先扫引言和目录，再读 §5，了解深度学习做自动化机制设计的路线。\n\n[Automated Mechanism Design: A Survey](https://www.sigecom.org/exchanges/volume_22/2/CURRY.pdf)",
      "color": "#397766"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000022",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 552,
      "y": 1678,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 竞价买的是哪种影响力\n\n*Neuron Auctions* 把广告主买到的影响力定义在模型内部。对照会议里的 token auction，记下两篇分别在竞价什么。\n\n[LLM Advertisement based on Neuron Auctions](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.08326) · [会议讨论的 token auction 论文](https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.10826)",
      "color": "#396A9A"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000023",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 552,
      "y": 1997,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 广告效果怎么进入定价\n\n读 *Evaluating and Pricing*，看作者如何估计点击意向，以及这个估计如何进入支付规则。把代理指标和实际点击分开记。\n\n[Evaluating and Pricing Advertisements in AI-Generated Responses](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.27686)",
      "color": "#396A9A"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000024",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 552,
      "y": 2316,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 广告能不能在生成后插入\n\n读 *PILA*，了解原回答生成后，由独立模块改写并插入广告的做法。用它对照生成过程中的广告机制。\n\n[PILA: Plug-and-Play Insertion for LLM-native Advertising](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25590)",
      "color": "#396A9A"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000028",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1087,
      "y": 1678,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 核对生成式推荐已有综述\n\n如果新综述要把推荐写进去，先看这篇综述如何组织数据、模型和任务，尤其是对话式推荐覆盖到了哪里。\n\n[A Survey on Generative Recommendation: Data, Model, and Tasks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.27157)",
      "color": "#95723E"
    },
    {
      "id": "0000000000000029",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1087,
      "y": 1997,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 核对广告安全已有框架\n\nQiu 与 Mei 按品牌提及、信息呈现、行为引导和长期偏好梳理生成式广告的商业影响。适合用来判断安全议题如何纳入。\n\n[Generative AI Advertising as a Problem of Trustworthy Commercial Intervention](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.18673)",
      "color": "#95723E"
    },
    {
      "id": "000000000000002a",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1087,
      "y": 2316,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 236,
      "text": "### 看一个推荐安全的例子\n\n*Loyal Agents* 的 Commerce Guidance 子集包含购物等推荐场景。看用户委托的代理遇到外部商业影响时，如何保护用户利益。\n\n[Loyal Agents · 论文全文](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.34714v1)",
      "color": "#95723E"
    }
  ],
